menuconfig AS5600
    bool "AS5600 magnetic rotary encoder (polled I2C keymap sensor)"
    default y
    depends on DT_HAS_NIKOLAS_AS5600_ENABLED
    depends on I2C
    help
      Driver for the AS5600 12-bit magnetic angle sensor used as a ZMK keymap
      encoder. Polls the RAW ANGLE register over I2C on its own thread and
      reports rotation deltas (in degrees) on SENSOR_CHAN_ROTATION.

if AS5600

config AS5600_THREAD_STACK_SIZE
    int "AS5600 poll thread stack size"
    default 2048
    help
      The poll thread is the context in which ZMK raises the sensor event and
      synchronously runs the bound behaviour chain (key press / scroll), so it
      needs enough headroom for that whole call depth — 1024 was marginal.

config AS5600_THREAD_PRIORITY
    int "AS5600 poll thread priority"
    default 10
    help
      Preemptible priority of the polling thread. The thread sleeps between
      reads, so a low priority is fine.

config AS5600_STARTUP_DELAY_MS
    int "AS5600 startup delay (ms)"
    default 1000
    help
      Delay before the poll thread first touches the (shared) I2C bus, giving
      the OLED, BLE and USB time to finish initialising first.

config AS5600_SMOOTHING_SHIFT
    int "AS5600 low-pass smoothing (alpha = 1/2^SHIFT)"
    default 1
    help
      Strength of the wrap-aware EMA applied to the raw angle. 0 disables it
      (raw passthrough); 1 = alpha 1/2 (light); 2 = alpha 1/4 (more). Higher
      values smooth more but add a little latency. Light smoothing lets the
      deadband below be smaller without spurious events creeping back.

config AS5600_DEADBAND_COUNTS
    int "AS5600 stillness deadband (12-bit counts)"
    default 4
    help
      Movement within this many counts of the reference angle is treated as
      sensor jitter, not motion. Stops the still magnet's angle noise from
      raising spurious sensor events that would keep ZMK from going idle (so the
      display blanks and the board can deep-sleep). Raise it if the display
      still won't blank at rest; lower it if very slow turns feel unresponsive.

endif # AS5600
